---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";
---

<DocsLayout title="Quick Start">
  <h1>Quick Start</h1>
  <p>Start Redis and the quota service locally, then inspect service health.</p>

  <h2>1. Start the stack</h2>
  <Code code={`docker compose up -d --build`} lang="bash" />

  <h2>2. Check Redis readiness</h2>
  <Code code={`grpcurl -plaintext localhost:28080 \\
  quota.v1.QuotaService/GetRedisStatus '{}'`} lang="bash" />

  <h2>3. Validate an example limit file</h2>
  <Code code={`docker compose run --rm quota-service \\
  quota-service validate-limits /app/examples/limits/workspace-email.yaml`} lang="bash" />

  <h2>4. Make a known-cost decision</h2>
  <Code code={`grpcurl -plaintext -d '{
  "request_id": "req_email_123",
  "context": {"product": "workspace", "environment": "local"},
  "action": "workspace.email.recipients",
  "cost": 25,
  "limits": [{
    "limit_id": "user_email_recipients_daily",
    "scope_key": "user:user_123",
    "action": "workspace.email.recipients",
    "unit": "recipients",
    "algorithm": "ALGORITHM_FIXED_WINDOW_CALENDAR",
    "window": {
      "type": "WINDOW_TYPE_CALENDAR",
      "calendar_unit": "CALENDAR_UNIT_DAY",
      "timezone": "UTC"
    },
    "limit": 500
  }]
}' localhost:28080 quota.v1.QuotaService/Consume`} lang="bash" />

  <h2>5. Inspect metrics</h2>
  <Code code={`curl -s http://localhost:29090/metrics | head`} lang="bash" />
</DocsLayout>
